# Testing and DTO Rules

## Mandatory Testing Stack

- Use `Vitest` for all non-E2E automated tests (backend unit/integration, frontend unit/component).
- Use `Playwright` only for end-to-end flows.
- Do not add new Jest-based tests or Jest configuration.
- If legacy Jest artifacts are encountered, migrate or replace them with Vitest coverage in the same change scope.

## Backend Endpoint Test Environment

- Backend endpoint tests must run in the dedicated test environment (Docker test containers), not against host processes.
- Use the test compose stack from `infra/compose/test.yml`.
- Seed and migrate the test database before endpoint/integration test runs when backend persistence is involved.

## DTO and Contract Policy (Zod-First)

- Zod is the primary and currently only supported DTO validation mechanism for new backend request/response contracts.
- New backend request validation must be implemented with explicit Zod schemas and inferred types from the same source.
- Keep contract artifacts serializable and framework-agnostic so they can be reused safely outside Nest runtime code.
- When frontend needs shared contract artifacts, import them from `@contracts/*` (mapped to `apps/backend/src/contracts/*`) and avoid deep imports from backend runtime modules.

## Session Environment Conventions

- Backend session runtime requires:
  - `SESSION_COOKIE_DOMAIN` (non-empty string)
  - `IDLE_TIMEOUT` (positive integer, seconds)
- Test environment values must be supplied through:
  - `TEST_SESSION_COOKIE_DOMAIN` -> mapped to backend `SESSION_COOKIE_DOMAIN`
  - `TEST_IDLE_TIMEOUT` -> mapped to backend `IDLE_TIMEOUT`
